c456592d-e55a-428b-81d1-1b2c5009ce1f	a4e9b4be-da98-4f9f-b662-fe288aa81847	e43866cd-4d5d-400a-81ee-69fff884ea8a	Otlhe Chakalisa	Science	1. Metamorphic rocks are formed from emended pressure and heat \n\n2. Sedimentary rocks are formed from other rocks breaking into sediments due to erosion then the sediment rock build into layers and layers \n\n3. Igneous rocks are formed from lava/magma cooling forming an intrusive/extrusive igneous rocks \n\n4.fossils are formed from an animal or plant is buried quickly in a place where there is very little air,sometimes the imprint of an animal or plant is left that is a mould but when the mould fills with minerals that harden it is called a cast	2026-03-18 14:00:37.788798	2026-03-18 14:00:37.788798
b6d714f2-a0d2-42b2-8d68-b3e392e214f3	a4e9b4be-da98-4f9f-b662-fe288aa81847	e43866cd-4d5d-400a-81ee-69fff884ea8a	Otlhe Chakalisa	Science	Thermal and electrical conductors also insulators  \n1. Thermal conductors-they are thermal conductors such as copper,aluminium,iron,graphite.as u know that these materials that allow heat to flow through them easily \n\n2. Thermal insulators-these are materials  that resist heat flow eg wood ,plastic, air,wool.\n\nElectric conductors -these are materials that allow electricity to flow through them easily eg copper, aluminium,gold,graphite.\n\nElectric insulators-these materials don’t allow electricity to flow through them such as wood,plastic,air,wool,glass.	2026-03-18 14:38:22.97368	2026-03-18 14:38:22.97368
