": "What is the place value of the digit 2 in the number 102,304?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "In the number 102,304, the digit 2 is in the thousands place, which means its place value is 2,000.", "correctAnswer": "2,000"}, {"id": "q_1773069110257_13", "type": "true_false", "options": [], "question": "Rounding down means you decrease the value of a number.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Rounding down involves taking a number and reducing it to the nearest whole number or lower value.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773069110257_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "If the digit after the decimal point is 5, you will round ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "According to rounding rules, if the digit after the decimal is 5 or more, you round up the previous digit.", "correctAnswer": "up"}, {"id": "q_1773069110257_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "How is the place value of 8 in the number 58,914 determined?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The position of the digit in the number defines its place value.", "correctAnswer": "The place value is determined by its position, which is in the thousands place, making it 8,000."}, {"id": "q_1773069110257_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["9.4", "10.3", "9.5", "10.6"], "question": "Which of the following numbers rounded to the nearest whole number is 10?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "When rounding 9.5 to the nearest whole number, since it is exactly halfway, it rounds up to 10.", "correctAnswer": "9.5"}, {"id": "q_1773069110257_17", "type": "true_false", "options": [], "question": "The digit 0 in the number 1,205 has a place value of 0.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "While the digit 0 indicates no value, its place value in the context of the number is 0, but it plays a role in defining the place of the other digits.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773069110257_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The number 12.3 rounded to 