ssel returns blood to the heart?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Veins are the blood vessels that carry deoxygenated blood back to the heart after delivering oxygen to the body's tissues.", "correctAnswer": "Veins"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_6", "type": "true_false", "question": "Red blood cells are responsible for carrying oxygen.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Red blood cells contain hemoglobin, which binds to oxygen in the lungs and transports it to the tissues.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_7", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The _______ is the largest artery in the body.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The aorta is the main artery that carries oxygenated blood from the heart to the rest of the body.", "correctAnswer": "aorta"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Regulating body temperature", "Producing hormones", "Digesting food", "Absorbing nutrients"], "question": "Which of the following is a function of the circulatory system?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The circulatory system helps regulate body temperature by adjusting blood flow to the skin and extremities.", "correctAnswer": "Regulating body temperature"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_9", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name the component of blood that helps in clotting.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Platelets are small cell fragments in the blood that play a key role in clotting and preventing excessive bleeding.", "correctAnswer": "platelets"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_10", "type": "true_false", "question": "The heart has four chambers.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The human heart has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles, which work together to pump blood.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_11", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Arteries", "Veins", "Capillaries", "Aorta"], "question": "Which blood vessel is responsible for exchanging substances with tissues?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Capillaries are tiny blood vessels that allow for the exchange of oxygen, carbon dioxide, nutrients, and waste between blood and tissues.", "correctAnswer": "Capillaries"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_12", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The _______ carries deoxygenated blood from the body back to the heart.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The vena cava is a large vein that carries deoxygenated blood from the body back to the heart.", "correctAnswer": "vena cava"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_13", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the main function of the valves in the heart?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Heart valves ensure that blood flows in one direction and prevent it from flowing backward.", "correctAnswer": "to prevent backflow of blood"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_14", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Oxygen-rich", "Oxygen-poor", "Carbon dioxide-rich", "Nutrient-rich"], "question": "What type of blood is found in the pulmonary veins?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Pulmonary veins carry oxygen-rich blood from the lungs back to the heart.", "correctAnswer": "Oxygen-rich"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_15", "type": "true_false", "question": "The heart is located in the abdomen.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The heart is located in the thoracic cavity, between the lungs, not in the abdomen.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_16", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The _______ is the smallest type of blood vessel.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Capillaries are the smallest blood vessels, allowing for the exchange of gases and nutrients at the cellular level.", "correctAnswer": "capillary"}, {"id": "q_1773135809153_17", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the term for the liquid part of blood that contains water, salts, and proteins?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Plasma is the liquid component of blood that carries cells, nutrients, hormones, and waste products.", "correctAnswer": "plasma"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:43:29.166817	\N
