": "The term 'kitten' refers to a young cat, which typically is very small and playful.", "correctAnswer": "kitten"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What do you call the person who writes books?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An author is someone who creates and writes books, stories, or other literary works.", "correctAnswer": "Author"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Elephant", "Tiger", "Lion", "Giraffe"], "question": "Which animal is known as the king of the jungle?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The lion is often referred to as the king of the jungle due to its strength and position as a top predator.", "correctAnswer": "Lion"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Earth is flat.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The Earth is an oblate spheroid, meaning it is mostly spherical but slightly flattened at the poles.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The opposite of 'hot' is ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Cold is the opposite of hot, describing lower temperatures in weather and substances.", "correctAnswer": "cold"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the largest mammal in the world?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The blue whale is the largest mammal and indeed the largest animal known to have ever existed on Earth.", "correctAnswer": "Blue whale"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Green", "Purple", "Red", "Orange"], "question": "Which of these is a primary color?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Red is one of the three primary colors (along with blue and yellow) from which all other colors can be created.", "correctAnswer": "Red"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "A triangle has four sides.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A triangle is defined as a polygon with three sides and three angles.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process of plants making their food is called ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen.", "correctAnswer": "photosynthesis"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the main language spoken in the United States?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "English is the most widely spoken language in the United States, used in government, media, and education.", "correctAnswer": "English"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Lion", "Wolf", "Dog", "Fox"], "question": "Which of these is a domesticated animal?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Dogs are domesticated animals that have been bred by humans for thousands of years for companionship and work.", "correctAnswer": "Dog"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Great Wall of China is visible from space.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The Great Wall is not easily visible from space without aid; it blends in with the natural landscape.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773138545017_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The ______ is the largest organ in the human body.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The skin is the largest organ of the body, serving as a protective barrier and regulating temperature.", "correctAnswer": "skin"}]	none	2026-03-10 10:29:05.029479	\N
