n": "Venus is hotter than Mercury.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Despite being farther from the Sun, Venus has a thick atmosphere that traps heat, making it hotter than Mercury.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773135810484_7", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The _______ is a belt of asteroids located between Mars and Jupiter.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The Asteroid Belt is located between Mars and Jupiter, containing many small rocky bodies that did not form into a planet.", "correctAnswer": "Asteroid Belt"}, {"id": "q_1773135810484_8", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What do we call the path that planets take around the Sun?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The path that planets follow around the Sun is called an orbit, which is determined by the gravitational pull of the Sun.", "correctAnswer": "Orbit"}, {"id": "q_1773135810484_9", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Earth", "Pluto", "Mars", "Jupiter"], "question": "Which of the following is a dwarf planet?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Pluto is classified as a dwarf planet because it does not clear its orbit of other debris, which is one of the criteria for full planet status.", "correctAnswer": "Pluto"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:43:30.498119	\N
