ne or more cells, which is a fundamental concept in biology.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773136096490_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In plants, the green pigment responsible for photosynthesis is called ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Chlorophyll is important for absorbing light energy during photosynthesis, allowing plants to convert sunlight into food.", "correctAnswer": "chlorophyll"}, {"id": "q_1773136096490_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name the molecule that carries genetic information.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is the molecule that contains the genetic blueprint for the development and function of living organisms.", "correctAnswer": "DNA"}, {"id": "q_1773136096490_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Protein", "Carbohydrate", "Lipid", "Vitamin"], "question": "Which of the following is NOT a type of macromolecule?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Vitamins are organic molecules that are essential in small quantities for life but are not classified as macromolecules like proteins, carbohydrates, and lipids.", "correctAnswer": "Vitamin"}, {"id": "q_1773136096490_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Bacteria are prokaryotic cells.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Bacteria are classified as prokaryotic cells because they do not have a nucleus and their genetic material is not membrane-bound.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:48:16.503199	\N
