_false", "question": "Ethernet is a type of wireless network technology.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Ethernet is a wired networking technology used for connecting devices in a LAN, not a wireless technology.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136486928_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In networking, the term ______ refers to the maximum data transfer rate of a network.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Bandwidth is the maximum rate of data transfer across a network, influencing how fast information can be sent and received.", "correctAnswer": "bandwidth"}, {"id": "q_1773136486928_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name one advantage of using a wireless network.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "One of the main advantages of a wireless network is mobility, allowing users to connect to the network from different locations without being tethered by cables.", "correctAnswer": "Mobility"}, {"id": "q_1773136486928_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Virtual Private Network", "Variable Public Network", "Virtual Public Network", "Very Private Network"], "question": "What does the acronym VPN stand for?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A VPN, or Virtual Private Network, creates a secure connection over the internet, allowing users to access private networks remotely.", "correctAnswer": "Virtual Private Network"}, {"id": "q_1773136486928_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "A modem is used to connect a network to the internet.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A modem (modulator-demodulator) converts digital data from a computer into an analog signal for transmission over phone lines or cable, connecting the network to the internet.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:54:46.941879	\N
