 and non-renewable resource, whereas solar, wind, and hydropower are renewable energy sources that can be replenished naturally.", "correctAnswer": "Natural Gas"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "The pH scale ranges from 0 to 14, with 7 being neutral.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The pH scale indeed ranges from 0 to 14, where values below 7 indicate acidity, values above 7 indicate alkalinity, and 7 is neutral.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The chemical formula for water is ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Water is composed of two hydrogen atoms covalently bonded to one oxygen atom, represented by the chemical formula H2O.", "correctAnswer": "H2O"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the main function of the mitochondria in a cell?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Mitochondria play a key role in energy metabolism, converting nutrients into ATP, which is essential for various cellular functions.", "correctAnswer": "The mitochondria are known as the powerhouse of the cell, as they produce ATP through cellular respiration, providing energy for cellular activities."}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Roots", "Stems", "Leaves", "Flowers"], "question": "Which structure in plants is primarily responsible for photosynthesis?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Leaves contain chlorophyll and are the main site for photosynthesis, where sunlight is captured to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose.", "correctAnswer": "Leaves"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Earth revolves around the Sun in a perfect circle.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Earth's orbit around the Sun is elliptical, meaning it is an oval shape rather than a perfect circle.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The basic unit of life is the ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Cells are the fundamental building blocks of all living organisms, serving as the basic unit of structure and function.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Describe the process of natural selection.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Natural selection is a key mechanism of evolution, explaining how species adapt to their environments through inherited traits.", "correctAnswer": "Natural selection is the process where organisms better adapted to their environment tend to survive and produce more offspring, leading to evolutionary changes over time."}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Carbon", "Neon", "Sodium", "Chlorine"], "question": "Which of the following elements is essential for the formation of proteins?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Carbon is a fundamental building block of life and is essential for forming proteins, which are made up of amino acids containing carbon.", "correctAnswer": "Carbon"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "All mammals are warm-blooded.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This statement is true; all mammals are endothermic, maintaining a constant body temperature regardless of environmental conditions.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The force that pulls objects toward the center of the Earth is called ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Gravity is the force of attraction that pulls objects towards the center of the Earth, influencing movement and stability.", "correctAnswer": "gravity"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the significance of the water cycle?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The water cycle ensures that water is continuously available in different forms, which is essential for life on Earth.", "correctAnswer": "The water cycle is crucial for replenishing freshwater resources, regulating climate, and supporting ecosystems by cycling water through evaporation, condensation, and precipitation."}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Photosynthesis", "Fermentation", "Cellular Respiration", "Transpiration"], "question": "Which process involves the conversion of glucose into energy in the presence of oxygen?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Cellular respiration is the process by which cells convert glucose and oxygen into energy (ATP), carbon dioxide, and water.", "correctAnswer": "Cellular Respiration"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "Viruses are considered living organisms.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Viruses are not considered living organisms because they cannot carry out metabolic processes on their own and require a host cell to replicate.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136610474_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The organ responsible for pumping blood throughout the body is the ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the circulatory system, supplying oxygen and nutrients to tissues.", "correctAnswer": "heart"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:56:50.487678	\N
