ual in length and parallel, but not all sides need to be equal. A shape with all equal sides is a rhombus.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The formula to calculate the circumference of a circle is ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The circumference of a circle is calculated using the formula 2 times π (pi) times the radius (r). This is a key concept in geometry.", "correctAnswer": "2πr"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the value of x if 2x + 3 = 11?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "To solve for x, subtract 3 from both sides to get 2x = 8, then divide both sides by 2 to find x = 4.", "correctAnswer": "4"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["4", "6", "7", "8"], "question": "Which of the following is a prime number?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that cannot be formed by multiplying two smaller natural numbers. 7 is prime because it has no divisors other than 1 and itself.", "correctAnswer": "7"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The product of two negative numbers is positive.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "In arithmetic, the product of two negative numbers results in a positive number, which is a fundamental property of multiplication.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In the equation y = mx + b, m represents the ______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "In the slope-intercept form of a linear equation, m represents the slope, which indicates the steepness and direction of the line.", "correctAnswer": "slope"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 24 and 36?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The GCD of two numbers is the largest number that divides both of them without leaving a remainder. For 24 and 36, the GCD is 12.", "correctAnswer": "12"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["25", "30", "35", "40"], "question": "What is 15% of 200?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "To calculate 15% of 200, you multiply 200 by 0.15, resulting in 30. Understanding percentages is crucial in many real-world applications.", "correctAnswer": "30"}, {"id": "q_1773136658340_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "All triangles are congruent.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Not all triangles are congruent; congruency means that two triangles are identical in shape and size. Triangles can vary in dimensions while still being triangles.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:57:38.353309	\N
