ion) model consists of seven layers, each representing different network functions.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "A _______ is an address that uniquely identifies a device on a network.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A MAC address (Media Access Control address) is a unique identifier assigned to network interfaces for communications on the physical network segment.", "correctAnswer": "MAC address"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What does DNS stand for?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "DNS stands for Domain Name System, which translates domain names into IP addresses, allowing users to access websites easily.", "correctAnswer": "Domain Name System"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Router", "Switch", "Repeater", "Hub"], "question": "Which device is typically used to amplify or regenerate signals in a network?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A repeater amplifies or regenerates signals to extend the range of a network connection.", "correctAnswer": "Repeater"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Firewalls are used to protect networks from unauthorized access.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Firewalls monitor and control incoming and outgoing network traffic based on predetermined security rules.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In a wireless network, the _______ is the device that transmits data wirelessly.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An access point serves as a hub for wireless connections, allowing devices to connect to a wired network wirelessly.", "correctAnswer": "access point"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is bandwidth in the context of networking?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Bandwidth indicates the capacity of a network to transmit data, typically measured in bits per second.", "correctAnswer": "Bandwidth refers to the maximum rate of data transfer across a network."}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Connects devices", "Modulates and demodulates signals", "Routes data", "Stores data"], "question": "What is the main function of a modem?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A modem modulates digital signals from a computer to analog for transmission over phone lines and demodulates incoming signals back to digital.", "correctAnswer": "Modulates and demodulates signals"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "Ethernet is a type of wireless networking technology.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Ethernet is a wired networking technology that uses cables to connect devices in a local area network (LAN).", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "A _______ is a unique string of numbers separated by dots that identifies a specific device on the internet.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An IP address is a numerical label assigned to each device connected to a computer network that uses the Internet Protocol for communication.", "correctAnswer": "IP address"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the purpose of network topology?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Understanding network topology helps in designing and managing the network efficiently.", "correctAnswer": "Network topology describes the arrangement of different elements (links, nodes, etc.) in a computer network."}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["HTTP", "HTTPS", "FTP", "SMTP"], "question": "Which of the following protocols is used for secure data transmission over the internet?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "HTTPS (HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure) is used for secure communication over a computer network, especially the internet.", "correctAnswer": "HTTPS"}, {"id": "q_1773136718361_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "VPN stands for Virtual Private Network.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A VPN (Virtual Private Network) creates a secure connection over a less secure network, such as the internet.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-10 09:58:38.372942	\N
