iptical, not a perfect circle, making this statement false.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The smallest unit of life is called a ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A cell is the fundamental structural and functional unit of all living organisms.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name the planet known as the 'Red Planet'.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Mars is often referred to as the 'Red Planet' due to its reddish appearance caused by iron oxide (rust) on its surface.", "correctAnswer": "Mars"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["0°C", "50°C", "100°C", "150°C"], "question": "What is the boiling point of water at sea level?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The boiling point of water at sea level is 100°C (212°F). This is a standard physical property of water.", "correctAnswer": "100°C"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The human body has four lungs.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Humans have two lungs, which are essential for respiration, making this statement false.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process of converting a liquid to a gas is called ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Evaporation is the process where liquid molecules gain enough energy to transition into a gaseous state.", "correctAnswer": "evaporation"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the main gas found in the Earth's atmosphere?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Nitrogen makes up about 78% of Earth's atmosphere, making it the most abundant gas present.", "correctAnswer": "Nitrogen"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Liver", "Lung", "Heart", "Kidney"], "question": "Which organ is responsible for pumping blood throughout the body?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The heart is the organ that pumps blood through the circulatory system, supplying oxygen and nutrients to the body.", "correctAnswer": "Heart"}, {"id": "q_1773136835389_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "Invertebrates are animals that have a backbone.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Invertebrates are animals that lack a backbone. Examples include insects, arachnids, and mollusks.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-10 10:00:35.401878	\N
