ue of pi (π) rounded to two decimal places?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Pi is a mathematical constant approximately equal to 3.14 when rounded to two decimal places.", "correctAnswer": "3.14"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["5", "6", "7", "8"], "question": "What is 30 divided by 5?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Dividing 30 by 5 gives you 6, as 5 times 6 equals 30.", "correctAnswer": "6"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "All squares are rectangles.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A square is a special type of rectangle where all sides are equal and angles are right angles.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The area of a rectangle is calculated by multiplying its length by its ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The area formula for a rectangle is length × width, which gives the total space within the rectangle.", "correctAnswer": "width"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the smallest prime number?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The smallest prime number is 2, which is the only even prime number and has only two divisors: 1 and itself.", "correctAnswer": "2"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["90", "45", "180", "360"], "question": "How many degrees are in a right angle?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A right angle measures exactly 90 degrees, which is a standard measurement in geometry.", "correctAnswer": "90"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "A hexagon has six sides.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "By definition, a hexagon is a polygon with six sides and six angles.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773137030715_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The perimeter of a square is calculated by multiplying the length of one side by ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "e