ube that connects the larynx to the bronchi, allowing air to pass into the lungs.", "correctAnswer": "Trachea"}, {"id": "q_1773166740569_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "Carbon dioxide is a waste product of respiration.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "During cellular respiration, oxygen is used to produce energy, and carbon dioxide is generated as a waste product. This carbon dioxide is then expelled from the body through the respiratory system.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773166740569_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The tiny air sacs in the lungs where gas exchange occurs are called ______.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Alveoli are small, balloon-like structures that increase the surface area for gas exchange, allowing oxygen to enter the blood and carbon dioxide to be removed.", "correctAnswer": "alveoli"}, {"id": "q_1773166740569_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name the process by which we breathe in air.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Inhalation is the process of taking air into the lungs, which occurs when the diaphragm contracts and expands the thoracic cavity.", "correctAnswer": "Inhalation"}, {"id": "q_1773166740569_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["To filter air", "To produce mucus", "To expand the lungs", "To transport oxygen"], "question": "What is the role of the cilia in the respiratory system?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Cilia are tiny hair-like structures that line the respiratory tract. They help to trap and move particles and pathogens out of the airways, keeping the lungs clean.", "correctAnswer": "To filter air"}, {"id": "q_1773166740569_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The nasal cavity is not involved in the process of breathing.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The nasal cavity plays a crucial role in breathing by filtering, warming, and humidifying the air before it enters the lungs.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-10 18:19:00.697841	\N
