ps in maintaining soil fertility."}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Ionic bond", "Covalent bond", "Hydrogen bond", "Metallic bond"], "question": "Which type of bond is primarily responsible for the unique properties of water?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Hydrogen bonds are weak attractions between water molecules that lead to unique properties such as high surface tension, high specific heat, and solvent capabilities.", "correctAnswer": "Hydrogen bond"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "The theory of evolution by natural selection was proposed by Gregor Mendel.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The theory of evolution by natural selection was proposed by Charles Darwin, while Gregor Mendel is known for his foundational work in genetics.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ is the basic unit of life and the smallest entity that can carry out all life processes.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Cells are the fundamental units of life that perform various functions essential for the survival and reproduction of organisms.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Explain the role of enzymes in biochemical reactions.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Enzymes are crucial for metabolism, allowing reactions to occur at rates necessary for life without being consumed in the process.", "correctAnswer": "Enzymes act as catalysts that speed up biochemical reactions by lowering the activation energy required for the reaction to proceed."}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Energy production", "Protein synthesis", "DNA replication", "Cell division"], "question": "Which of the following best describes the main function of ribosomes in a cell?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Ribosomes are cellular structures where proteins ar