nerates electric currents, which in turn produce the magnetic field surrounding the planet.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ hypothesis suggests that the universe is expanding over time.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The Big Bang hypothesis posits that the universe began from a singularity and has been expanding ever since, influencing the current structure and dynamics of the cosmos.", "correctAnswer": "Big Bang"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Discuss the impact of climate change on biodiversity.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "As temperatures rise and weather patterns change, many species struggle to adapt, leading to shifts in populations and potentially irreversible losses in biodiversity.", "correctAnswer": "Climate change significantly impacts biodiversity by altering habitats, disrupting ecosystems, and causing species extinction due to changing climates and human activities."}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Oxygen", "Nitrogen", "Carbon dioxide", "Argon"], "question": "Which of the following is a greenhouse gas that contributes to global warming?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Carbon dioxide is a major greenhouse gas that traps heat in the atmosphere, contributing to the greenhouse effect and global warming.", "correctAnswer": "Carbon dioxide"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "All isotopes of an element have the same number of neutrons.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Isotopes of an element have the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons, which results in different atomic masses.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773168676986_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The law of __________ states that energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The law of conservation of en