: "0.25 liters"}, {"id": "q_1773214721587_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "A kilometer is longer than a mile.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This statement is false. A mile is approximately 1.609 kilometers, making a mile longer than a kilometer.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773214721587_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The area of a rectangle is calculated by multiplying its length by its ________.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The area of a rectangle is determined using the formula Area = Length × Width, where width is the other dimension of the rectangle.", "correctAnswer": "width"}, {"id": "q_1773214721587_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the formula for calculating the circumference of a circle?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The circumference (C) of a circle can be calculated using the formula C = 2πr, where r is the radius of the circle.", "correctAnswer": "C = 2πr"}, {"id": "q_1773214721587_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Inch", "Foot", "Pound", "Meter"], "question": "Which of the following is not a unit of measurement for length?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Pound is a unit of weight, while inch, foot, and meter are units of length. Understanding the different categories of measurement units is crucial.", "correctAnswer": "Pound"}, {"id": "q_1773214721587_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "A liter is equivalent to 1000 cubic centimeters.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This statement is true. One liter is defined as the volume of a cube that measures 10 centimeters on each side, which equals 1000 cubic centimeters.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-11 07:38:41.923575	\N
