"All blood types can receive blood from any other type.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Blood type compatibility is crucial for transfusions. For example, Type O is considered the universal donor, while Type AB is the universal recipient.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The part of blood responsible for immunity is __________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "White blood cells are essential for the immune response, helping to identify and destroy pathogens such as bacteria and viruses.", "correctAnswer": "white blood cells"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the average lifespan of a red blood cell?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Red blood cells typically live for about 120 days before they are recycled by the body.", "correctAnswer": "About 120 days"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Iron", "Calcium", "Potassium", "Sodium"], "question": "What is the primary component of hemoglobin?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Hemoglobin is a protein found in red blood cells that contains iron, which is crucial for binding and transporting oxygen.", "correctAnswer": "Iron"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Blood is considered a connective tissue.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Blood is classified as a connective tissue because it connects different parts of the body by transporting nutrients, gases, and waste.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process of blood cell formation is called __________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Hematopoiesis is the process by which the body produces blood cells, primarily occurring in the bone marrow.", "correctAnswer": "hematopoiesis"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the role of plasma in blood?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Plasma serves as the medium for carrying various substances, including nutrients, hormones, and waste products throughout the body.", "correctAnswer": "Transport nutrients and waste"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Vitamin A", "Vitamin B12", "Vitamin K", "Vitamin C"], "question": "Which vitamin is essential for the synthesis of clotting factors?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Vitamin K is crucial for the synthesis of proteins that mediate blood clotting, making it essential for proper hemostasis.", "correctAnswer": "Vitamin K"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "The human body has 4 liters of blood on average.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An average adult human has about 5 to 6 liters of blood in their body, which constitutes about 7-8% of their total body weight.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The main function of platelets is to __________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Platelets are vital for the blood clotting process, helping to prevent excessive bleeding when injuries occur.", "correctAnswer": "clot blood"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the function of antibodies?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Antibodies are proteins produced by the immune system that specifically recognize and neutralize foreign objects like bacteria and viruses.", "correctAnswer": "Identify and neutralize pathogens"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["6.0 - 6.5", "7.0 - 7.5", "7.35 - 7.45", "8.0 - 8.5"], "question": "What is the pH range of human blood?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The normal pH range of human blood is 7.35 to 7.45, which is crucial for maintaining various physiological functions.", "correctAnswer": "7.35 - 7.45"}, {"id": "q_1773214730020_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "Blood type is determined by the presence of antigens on red blood cells.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Blood type is determined by the specific antigens present on the surface of red blood cells, which can trigger immune responses.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-11 07:38:50.355576	\N
