s a fundamental term for anyone learning the language.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Fill in the blank: 'Nous _______ (to eat) une pizza.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Mangeons' is the correct form of the verb 'manger' (to eat) in the present tense for 'nous' (we).", "correctAnswer": "mangeons"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Translate the sentence 'I love you' into French.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The phrase 'Je t'aime' translates to 'I love you' in French and is an important expression of affection.", "correctAnswer": "Je t'aime"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Village", "Ville", "Bourg", "Cité"], "question": "What is the French term for 'city'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Ville' is the correct term for 'city' in French. It is used in various contexts to refer to urban areas.", "correctAnswer": "Ville"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The French word 'mer' means 'land'.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Mer' actually means 'sea' in French. The word for 'land' is 'terre'. Understanding these basic vocabulary terms is essential for learners.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Complete the sentence: 'Il fait _______ (cold) aujourd'hui.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Froid' is the French word for 'cold', which is used to describe weather conditions.", "correctAnswer": "froid"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the French word for 'friend'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Ami' is the masculine form of 'friend' in French. For a female friend, the word is 'amie'.", "correctAnswer": "Ami"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Bonsoir", "Bonjour", "Bonne nuit", "Salut"], "question": "Which of the following is the correct translation for 'good morning'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Bonjour' is the correct way to say 'good morning' in French. It is a common greeting used during the day.", "correctAnswer": "Bonjour"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "In French, adjectives generally come before the nouns they describe.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "In French, most adjectives come after the nouns, although some common adjectives can precede the noun. This is a key grammatical rule.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Complete the phrase: 'Elle est très _______ (intelligent)'.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Intelligente' is the feminine form of 'intelligent' in French. Adjectives must agree in gender and number with the nouns they modify.", "correctAnswer": "intelligente"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the past participle of the verb 'aller' (to go) in French?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The past participle of 'aller' is 'allé', which is used to form compound tenses in French.", "correctAnswer": "allé"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Écouter", "Parler", "Dire", "Manger"], "question": "Which word means 'to speak' in French?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Parler' is the verb that means 'to speak' in French, which is essential for communication.", "correctAnswer": "Parler"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "The French word 'voiture' means 'train'.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Voiture' means 'car' in French. The word for 'train' is 'train'. Understanding transport vocabulary is important.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Fill in the blanks: 'Je veux _______ (to drink) de l'eau.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Boire' is the infinitive form of the verb 'to drink' in French and is used to express desires.", "correctAnswer": "boire"}, {"id": "q_1773215051125_19", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Translate 'They are happy' into French.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The phrase 'Ils sont heureux' translates to 'They are happy' in French, demonstrating subject-verb agreement.", "correctAnswer": "Ils sont heureux"}]	none	2026-03-11 07:44:11.468822	\N
8c9607a4-78a9-44c7-9d91-ad607bd33c25	6e9708f5-9912-4734-b267-d41ec837a114	Computer Science - Hard	Computer Science	hard	[{"id": "q_1773215136017_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["O(log n)", "O(n)", "O(n log n)", "O(1)"], "question": "Which of the following algorithms has the best average-case time complexity for searching in a balanced binary search tree?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "In a balanced binary search tree, the height of the tree is kept logarithmic in relation to the number of elements, leading to a search time complexity of O(log n) on average.", "correctAnswer": "O(log n)"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Big O notation can express both the upper and lower bounds of an algorithm's runtime.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Big O notation specifically describes the upper bound or worst-case scenario of an algorithm's time complexity, while lower bounds are expressed using Big Omega notation.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The ________ principle states that a software component should have only one reason to change.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The Single Responsibility Principle is part of SOLID principles in object-oriented design, emphasizing that a class should only have one job or responsibility, making it easier to maintain and understand.", "correctAnswer": "Single Responsibility"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Explain the difference between synchronous and asynchronous programming.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "In synchronous programming, the execution flow is linear and tasks must complete before moving to the next one, while asynchronous programming improves performance and responsiveness by allowing other tasks to run in the meantime.", "correctAnswer": "Synchronous programming executes tasks sequentially, blocking subsequent tasks until the current task is completed. Asynchronous programming allows tasks to run concurrently, enabling other operations to proceed without waiting for the current task to finish."}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Array", "HashMap", "Linked List", "HashMap and Doubly Linked List"], "question": "Which data structure is typically used to implement a LRU (Least Recently Used) cache?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "An LRU cache is most efficiently implemented using a combination of a HashMap for O(1) access time and a Doubly Linked List to keep track of the order of usage, allowing quick updates.", "correctAnswer": "HashMap and Doubly Linked List"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "In object-oriented programming, inheritance allows a class to inherit properties and methods from another class.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Inheritance is a fundamental concept in object-oriented programming that allows a new class (derived class) to inherit attributes and behaviors (methods) from an existing class (base class), promoting code reuse.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In SQL, the __________ clause is used to filter records that fulfill a specified condition.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The WHERE clause in SQL is essential for specifying the criteria for selecting records from a database, allowing for targeted data retrieval based on conditions.", "correctAnswer": "WHERE"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the purpose of a deadlock in operating systems, and how can it be resolved?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Understanding deadlocks is crucial in operating systems for managing processes efficiently. Solutions often involve careful resource management to prevent conditions that lead to deadlocks.", "correctAnswer": "A deadlock occurs when two or more processes are unable to proceed because each is waiting for the other to release resources. It can be resolved using techniques such as resource allocation graphs, deadlock detection, and prevention strategies like resource ordering or timeout."}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["A situation where two threads can read data simultaneously", "A situation where multiple threads modify shared data concurrently, leading to unpredictable results", "A method to synchronize access to shared resources", "A technique for optimizing thread execution"], "question": "Which of the following best describes a 'race condition' in concurrent programming?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Race conditions occur when the outcome of a program depends on the sequence or timing of uncontrollable events, such as the concurrent modification of shared data by multiple threads.", "correctAnswer": "A situation where multiple threads modify shared data concurrently, leading to unpredictable results"}, {"id": "q_1773215136017_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "A stack is a data structure that follows the First In First Out (FIFO) principle.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "A stack follows the Last In First Out (LIFO) principle, meaning the last element added is the first to be removed, which is contrary to the FIFO principle of a queue.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-11 07:45:36.361755	\N
619b79b2-54d0-4a8b-93fa-5c71686530f1	74d0d3ca-7e39-442f-b93d-e5b2f31efa5c	world war 1 - Medium	world war 1	medium	[{"id": "q_1773215369415_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["The sinking of the Lusitania", "The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand", "The invasion of Belgium", "The Zimmermann Telegram"], "question": "Which event is commonly considered the trigger for the outbreak of World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria on June 28, 1914, is considered the catalyst for the start of World War I, leading Austria-Hungary to declare war on Serbia and initiating a chain reaction of alliances.", "correctAnswer": "The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Treaty of Versailles officially ended World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Treaty of Versailles, signed on June 28, 1919, formally ended World War I and imposed heavy reparations and territorial losses on Germany.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ was a military alliance between Germany, Austria-Hungary, and Italy before World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Triple Alliance was formed in 1882 and was a significant military pact that influenced the dynamics of Europe leading up to World War I.", "correctAnswer": "Triple Alliance"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What was the primary purpose of trench warfare during World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Trench warfare was used extensively on the Western Front, offering soldiers some protection from enemy fire while creating a stalemate situation.", "correctAnswer": "To provide protection for soldiers and to hold ground against enemy attacks."}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["To promote economic recovery", "To resolve international disputes peacefully", "To establish new borders", "To create military alliances"], "question": "What was the main purpose of the League of Nations, established after World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The League of Nations was created to provide a platform for resolving international conflicts and to promote peace, although it ultimately failed to prevent future wars.", "correctAnswer": "To resolve international disputes peacefully"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "The United States entered World War I in 1917 primarily due to unrestricted submarine warfare by Germany.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Germany's use of unrestricted submarine warfare, which threatened American lives and shipping, was a significant factor that led to the U.S. entry into World War I in April 1917.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ was the last major offensive by the Central Powers in 1918.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Spring Offensive, also known as the Ludendorff Offensive, was launched by Germany in March 1918 and aimed to achieve a decisive victory before American forces could fully arrive.", "correctAnswer": "Spring Offensive"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name one significant technological advancement introduced during World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "World War I saw the introduction of several technological advancements such as tanks, which changed the nature of ground warfare, and airplanes, which began to be used for reconnaissance and combat.", "correctAnswer": "Tanks, airplanes, or chemical warfare."}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["France", "Italy", "Germany", "United Kingdom"], "question": "Which of the following countries was NOT part of the Allies during World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Germany was part of the Central Powers, while France, Italy, and the United Kingdom were key members of the Allies.", "correctAnswer": "Germany"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Western Front was characterized by rapid movements and quick victories.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Western Front was marked by trench warfare and a stalemate, with little territorial gain over extended periods, contrasting with the rapid movements seen in other theaters.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The use of __________ gas was one of the new forms of warfare introduced during World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Poison gas, including chlorine and mustard gas, was used for the first time on a large scale during World War I, leading to horrific injuries and suffering.", "correctAnswer": "poison"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What was one major consequence of World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "World War I resulted in significant geopolitical changes, including the dissolution of empires and the establishment of new nations and borders, particularly in Eastern Europe.", "correctAnswer": "The redrawing of national borders in Europe or the rise of new nations."}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Battle of the Somme", "Battle of Verdun", "Battle of Argonne Forest", "Battle of Belleau Wood"], "question": "Which battle is often regarded as the bloodiest single day in American military history during World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Battle of the Somme, fought in 1916, is known for its staggering number of casualties, with over 57,000 British soldiers killed on the first day alone.", "correctAnswer": "Battle of the Somme"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "Woodrow Wilson proposed the Fourteen Points as a basis for peace negotiations after World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "U.S. President Woodrow Wilson introduced the Fourteen Points as a framework for peace negotiations, emphasizing self-determination and the formation of the League of Nations.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773215369415_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ was the major treaty that ended the state of war between Germany and the Allied Powers.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Treaty of Versailles was signed on June 28, 1919, and marked the formal end of World War I, establishing terms that would have lasting effects on Germany and Europe.", "correctAnswer": "Treaty of Versailles"}]	none	2026-03-11 07:49:29.764174	\N
