 "The diameter of a circle is twice the radius. Therefore, if the radius is 3, the diameter is 3 × 2 = 6.", "correctAnswer": "6"}, {"id": "q_1773215400865_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is 15 divided by 3?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "To divide 15 by 3, you find how many times 3 can go into 15, which is 5 times.", "correctAnswer": "5"}, {"id": "q_1773215400865_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["7", "8", "9", "10"], "question": "What is the next number in the sequence: 2, 4, 6, __?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The sequence increases by 2 each time. After 6, the next number is 6 + 2 = 8.", "correctAnswer": "8"}, {"id": "q_1773215400865_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Zero is a positive number.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Zero is neither positive nor negative; it is a neutral number in the number line.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-11 07:50:01.293172	\N
