03186f2f-91d0-4188-8cbc-e2d78f9238b7	fac4ba22-93f5-4d0f-8a22-4dd473cd2fb2	Photosynthesis  - Easy	Photosynthesis 	easy	[{"id": "q_1773249178328_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Chlorophyll", "Carotene", "Xanthophyll", "Melanin"], "question": "What is the primary pigment involved in photosynthesis?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Chlorophyll is the main pigment found in plants that captures light energy from the sun, which is essential for photosynthesis. It primarily absorbs blue and red light, reflecting green light, which is why plants appear green.", "correctAnswer": "Chlorophyll"}, {"id": "q_1773249178328_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "Photosynthesis occurs in the roots of plants.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Photosynthesis primarily occurs in the leaves of plants, where chloroplasts are abundant. The roots are responsible for water and nutrient absorption from the soil, not for photosynthesis.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773249178328_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In photosynthesis, carbon dioxide and water are converted into __________ and oxygen.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "During photosynthesis, plants convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose (a type of sugar) and oxygen using sunlight as energy. Glucose serves as an energy source for the plant.", "correctAnswer": "glucose"}, {"id": "q_1773249178328_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the overall equation for photosynthesis?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The overall equation summarizes the process of photosynthesis, showing that six molecules of carbon dioxide and six molecules of water, using light energy, produce one molecule of glucose and six molecules of oxygen.", "correctAnswer": "6CO2 + 6H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 + 6O2"}, {"id": "q_1773249178328_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Roots", "Stems", "Leaves", "Flowers"], "question": "Which part of the plant is primarily responsible for photosynthesis?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Leaves are the main site of photosynthesis in plants because they contain the highest concentration of chloroplasts, where the photosynthetic reactions take place.", "correctAnswer": "Leaves"}]	none	2026-03-11 17:12:58.33935	\N
