ingdom includes multicellular organisms that are primarily heterotrophic?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Animalia kingdom consists of multicellular, eukaryotic organisms that obtain nutrients by consuming other organisms, making them heterotrophic.", "correctAnswer": "Animalia"}, {"id": "q_1773251942907_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "Viruses display all 7 characteristics of life.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Viruses do not display any of the 7 characteristics of life, as they cannot reproduce independently or carry out metabolic processes outside of a host cell.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773251942907_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In mammals, the young typically develop in the __________ attached to the mother's placenta.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Mammals give birth to live young that develop inside the uterus, where they are nourished by the placenta, allowing for a more extended developmental period.", "correctAnswer": "uterus"}, {"id": "q_1773251942907_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name one major distinguishing feature of arthropods.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Arthropods are characterized by having a hard exoskeleton, which provides protection and support, as well as jointed appendages.", "correctAnswer": "Exoskeleton"}, {"id": "q_1773251942907_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Autotrophic", "Heterotrophic", "Saprophytic", "Parasitic"], "question": "What type of nutrition do fungi primarily exhibit?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Fungi primarily obtain nutrients through saprophytic nutrition, meaning they absorb nutrients from decomposing organic matter, playing a crucial role in ecosystems.", "correctAnswer": "Saprophytic"}, {"id": "q_1773251942907_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Insects have three pairs of legs attached to their thorax.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Insects are characterized by having three pairs of legs, which are indeed attached to the thorax, along with other distinctive body features.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	1fdfa09e-c27e-43fb-8962-f6ed58908b5e	2026-03-11 17:59:03.055343	\N
