cryption to protect data during transmission.", "correctAnswer": "HTTPS"}, {"id": "q_1773252284928_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "Phishing is a legitimate way to obtain user information.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Phishing is a malicious practice where attackers impersonate legitimate entities to trick individuals into providing sensitive information.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773252284928_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process of converting data into a secret code to prevent unauthorized access is known as __________.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Encryption is a crucial security technique that transforms readable data into a coded version, ensuring confidentiality.", "correctAnswer": "encryption"}, {"id": "q_1773252284928_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What does 'URL' stand for?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A URL is the address used to access resources on the internet, specifying the location of a resource as well as the protocol used to retrieve it.", "correctAnswer": "Uniform Resource Locator"}, {"id": "q_1773252284928_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Microsoft Word", "Adobe Photoshop", "Linux", "Windows 10"], "question": "Which of the following is an example of open-source software?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Linux is an open-source operating system, meaning its source code is available for anyone to use, modify, and distribute.", "correctAnswer": "Linux"}, {"id": "q_1773252284928_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "A firewall is used to protect a network by filtering incoming and outgoing traffic.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Firewalls serve as a barrier between trusted and untrusted networks, controlling the flow of data to enhance security.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-11 18:04:45.017115	\N
