ry was NOT a member of the Allies during World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Germany was part of the Central Powers, while the United Kingdom, France, and Russia were key members of the Allies fighting against them.", "correctAnswer": "Germany"}, {"id": "q_1773380500211_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "The use of chemical weapons was first introduced during World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "World War I saw the first large-scale use of chemical weapons in warfare, with chlorine gas being used by the Germans in 1915.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773380500211_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The ________ was the name of the German military strategy for a quick victory in World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Schlieffen Plan was Germany's strategy to quickly defeat France before turning to fight Russia, aiming to avoid a prolonged two-front war.", "correctAnswer": "Schlieffen Plan"}, {"id": "q_1773380500211_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name one major technological advancement in warfare that emerged during World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Tanks were developed during World War I to break through trench defenses, representing a significant technological advancement in warfare.", "correctAnswer": "Tanks"}, {"id": "q_1773380500211_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["To promote military alliances", "To prevent future wars", "To divide territories", "To regulate trade"], "question": "What was the primary purpose of the League of Nations established after World War I?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The League of Nations was created in 1920 to promote peace and cooperation among countries, aiming to prevent future conflicts following the devastation of World War I.", "correctAnswer": "To prevent future wars"}, {"id": "q_1773380500211_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Woodrow Wilson was the President of the United States during World War I.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Woodrow Wilson served as President of the United States from 1913 to 1921 and led the country through World War I.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-13 05:41:40.222321	\N
