r reflect on the differences between appearance and reality. It can convey deeper truths and evoke emotions, enhancing the overall impact of a story.", "correctAnswer": "Irony adds depth and complexity to a narrative by creating a contrast between expectation and reality. For example, in 'The Gift of the Magi' by O. Henry, the couple sacrifices their most prized possessions to buy gifts for each other, leading to a poignant twist."}, {"id": "q_1773253288876_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["The futility of ambition", "The power of love", "The importance of friendship", "The inevitability of fate"], "question": "Which of the following best describes the primary theme of Shakespeare's 'Macbeth'?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The central theme of 'Macbeth' is the destructive nature of unchecked ambition. Macbeth's desire for power leads him to commit regicide and ultimately results in his downfall, illustrating that ambition, when not tempered by moral considerations, can lead to ruin.", "correctAnswer": "The futility of ambition"}]	none	2026-03-11 18:21:28.981064	\N
