ecure data transmission over the internet?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "HTTPS (HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure) is an extension of HTTP that uses encryption to secure data transmitted between a user's browser and the web server.", "correctAnswer": "HTTPS"}, {"id": "q_1773296503113_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "Phishing is a method used to acquire sensitive information by masquerading as a trustworthy entity.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Phishing attacks often use deceptive emails or websites to trick users into providing personal information such as passwords or credit card numbers.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773296503113_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In programming, __________ is a technique used to hide the implementation details of an object.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Encapsulation is a fundamental concept in object-oriented programming that restricts access to certain components of an object, promoting modularity and reducing complexity.", "correctAnswer": "encapsulation"}, {"id": "q_1773296503113_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What does 'URL' stand for, and what is its purpose?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A URL is used to locate and access web pages and other resources on the internet, providing a standardized way to reference them.", "correctAnswer": "Uniform Resource Locator; it specifies the address of a resource on the internet."}, {"id": "q_1773296503113_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Data that is small enough to be processed by traditional tools", "Large volumes of data that cannot be processed efficiently with traditional tools", "Data that is always accurate and reliable", "Data that is only used for statistical analysis"], "question": "Which of the following best describes 'Big Data'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Big Data' refers to data sets that are so large or complex that traditional data processing applications are inadequa