": ["Carbon Dioxide", "Oxygen", "Nitrogen", "Hydrogen"], "question": "What gas do living beings breathe in to survive?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Oxygen is essential for the survival of most living organisms, as it is used in cellular respiration to generate energy.", "correctAnswer": "Oxygen"}, {"id": "q_1773296628976_6", "type": "true_false", "question": "All animals can fly.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Not all animals have the ability to fly; many species, including mammals, reptiles, and amphibians, do not possess this capability.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773296628976_7", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ is the basic unit of life.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The cell is often referred to as the basic unit of life because it is the smallest structure capable of performing all life functions.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773296628976_8", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the primary source of energy for the Earth?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The Sun provides the necessary energy for most life forms on Earth, driving processes such as photosynthesis and influencing climate.", "correctAnswer": "The Sun"}, {"id": "q_1773296628976_9", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Mars", "Jupiter", "Saturn", "Earth"], "question": "Which planet is known as the Red Planet?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Mars is often referred to as the Red Planet due to its reddish appearance, which is caused by iron oxide (rust) on its surface.", "correctAnswer": "Mars"}]	none	2026-03-12 06:23:48.987875	\N
