the relationships among all living organisms."}, {"id": "q_1773344062147_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Oxygen", "Carbon dioxide", "Nitrogen", "Hydrogen"], "question": "Which gas is primarily responsible for the greenhouse effect?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Carbon dioxide (CO2) is a significant greenhouse gas that traps heat in the atmosphere, contributing to global warming and climate change. Its increased concentration due to human activities is a major environmental concern.", "correctAnswer": "Carbon dioxide"}, {"id": "q_1773344062147_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "All living organisms are made up of cells.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The cell theory states that all living organisms are composed of one or more cells, which are the basic units of life. This principle is fundamental to biology and helps define the characteristics of living organisms.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773344062147_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The scientist known for the laws of motion and universal gravitation is __________.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Isaac Newton formulated the three laws of motion and the law of universal gravitation, laying the foundation for classical mechanics and significantly advancing the scientific revolution.", "correctAnswer": "Isaac Newton"}, {"id": "q_1773344062147_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What role do enzymes play in biological reactions?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Enzymes lower the activation energy needed for reactions to occur, which is crucial for sustaining life by enabling essential biochemical processes.", "correctAnswer": "Enzymes act as catalysts that speed up chemical reactions in the body without being consumed in the process, allowing metabolic pathways to proceed efficiently."}, {"id": "q_1773344062147_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["0", "7", "14", "10"], "question": "What is the pH level of pure water at 25 degrees Celsius?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Pure water has a neutral pH of 7 at 25 degrees Celsius, indicating that the concentration of hydrogen ions (H+) and hydroxide ions (OH-) is equal. This neutrality is key for many biological processes.", "correctAnswer": "7"}, {"id": "q_1773344062147_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "DNA is composed of amino acids.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is made up of nucleotides, which consist of a sugar, a phosphate group, and a nitrogenous base. Amino acids, on the other hand, are the building blocks of proteins, which are synthesized based on the genetic information encoded in DNA.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-12 19:34:22.159318	\N
