on", "Missense mutation", "Nonsense mutation", "Point mutation"], "question": "Which type of mutation involves the substitution of one nucleotide for another in a DNA sequence?", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "A point mutation is a change in a single nucleotide in the DNA sequence, which can result in a change to the amino acid sequence of a protein.", "correctAnswer": "Point mutation"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "All enzymes are proteins.", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "While most enzymes are proteins, some RNA molecules, known as ribozymes, also have catalytic activity.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ is a structure that regulates the movement of substances in and out of the cell.", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "The cell membrane, also known as the plasma membrane, is a selective barrier that controls the entry and exit of substances, maintaining homeostasis within the cell.", "correctAnswer": "cell membrane"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Explain the significance of genetic drift in evolution.", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "Genetic drift can have significant effects on the genetic makeup of a population over time, influencing evolutionary processes and species adaptation.", "correctAnswer": "Genetic drift is a mechanism of evolution that causes allele frequencies to change due to random sampling effects, especially in small populations, potentially leading to reduced genetic diversity."}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Metabolism", "Growth", "Reproduction", "Photosynthesis"], "question": "Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of all living organisms?", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "While photosynthesis is a characteristic of certain organisms, such as plants and some bacteria, not all living organisms can perform photosynthesis.", "correctAnswer": "Photosynthesis"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The structure of DNA is a double helix.", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "The DNA molecule is structured as a double helix, consisting of two strands that coil around each other, held together by base pairs.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ theory states that all living organisms are composed of cells.", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "The cell theory is a fundamental concept in biology that posits that all living things are made of cells, which are the basic unit of life.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the primary function of ribosomes in a cell?", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "Ribosomes play a crucial role in the process of translation, where they read mRNA sequences and assemble amino acids into proteins, essential for cellular function.", "correctAnswer": "Ribosomes are responsible for synthesizing proteins by translating messenger RNA (mRNA) into polypeptide chains."}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["To split water molecules", "To capture light energy", "To fix carbon dioxide into organic molecules", "To produce ATP"], "question": "What is the primary purpose of the Calvin cycle in photosynthesis?", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "The Calvin cycle is the phase of photosynthesis that converts carbon dioxide into glucose and other organic molecules using energy derived from ATP and NADPH produced in the light-dependent reactions.", "correctAnswer": "To fix carbon dioxide into organic molecules"}, {"id": "q_1773380443005_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "Natural selection leads to the evolution of species over time.", "difficulty": "expert", "explanation": "Natural selection is a key mechanism of evolution where individuals with advantageous 