mple of cloud storage, where data is stored on remote servers accessed via the internet, rather than on local devices.", "correctAnswer": "Google Drive"}, {"id": "q_1773555632442_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "A password should be easy to remember and simple to guess.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "False. A strong password should be complex and difficult to guess, typically combining letters, numbers, and symbols to enhance security.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773555632442_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "HTML stands for HyperText _________ Language.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language, which is the standard markup language used to create web pages.", "correctAnswer": "Markup"}, {"id": "q_1773555632442_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the primary purpose of an antivirus software?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Antivirus software is designed to detect, prevent, and remove malicious software, such as viruses and malware, from computers and networks.", "correctAnswer": "To protect computers from viruses and malware"}, {"id": "q_1773555632442_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Windows", "Linux", "Android", "Microsoft Office"], "question": "Which of the following is not an operating system?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Microsoft Office is a suite of productivity applications, not an operating system. Windows, Linux, and Android are all operating systems.", "correctAnswer": "Microsoft Office"}, {"id": "q_1773555632442_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "A URL is an address used to access resources on the internet.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "True. A URL (Uniform Resource Locator) is the address used to access web resources, directing browsers to specific locations on the internet.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-15 06:20:32.453739	\N
