es an adverb of time?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Yesterday' indicates when the action of finishing the project took place, making it an adverb of time.", "correctAnswer": "They finished their project yesterday."}, {"id": "q_1773565156592_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "All adverbs are used to modify verbs.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "While many adverbs modify verbs, some can modify adjectives and other adverbs.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773565156592_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "She stormed out of the room __________ (angrily).", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Angrily' describes how she stormed out of the room, functioning as an adverb of manner.", "correctAnswer": "angrily"}, {"id": "q_1773565156592_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the difference between adverbs of time and adverbs of manner?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This distinction is important for understanding how adverbs function in sentences.", "correctAnswer": "Adverbs of time indicate when an action occurs, while adverbs of manner describe how an action is performed."}, {"id": "q_1773565156592_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["quickly", "later", "rude", "angry"], "question": "Select the correct adverb of time for this sentence: 'They will arrive __________.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Later' indicates when they will arrive, thus it is an adverb of time.", "correctAnswer": "later"}, {"id": "q_1773565156592_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "The sentence 'She swims fast' contains an adverb of time.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Fast' describes how she swims, not when, so it is an adverb of manner.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773565156592_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "He will call you __________ (soon).", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Soon' indicates the time at which he will call, making it an adverb of time.", "correctAnswer": 