ghest degree of happiness.", "correctAnswer": "happiest"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "The sentence 'He is the most intelligent person in the room' uses a comparative form.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This sentence uses the superlative form 'most intelligent' to compare one person against all others in the room.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Fill in the blank: 'This movie is _____ exciting than the last one.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The word 'more' is correctly used before the adjective 'exciting' to form a comparative.", "correctAnswer": "more"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_7", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["He runs faster than anyone else.", "This is the most beautiful painting I've ever seen.", "She is smarter than her sister.", "They are the friendliest in the group."], "question": "Which of the following sentences correctly uses a superlative adjective?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The sentence uses 'most beautiful' to indicate that this painting is being compared to all others, which is correct for superlatives.", "correctAnswer": "This is the most beautiful painting I've ever seen."}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_8", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the comparative form of the adjective 'strong'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Stronger' is the comparative form used to compare the strength of two subjects.", "correctAnswer": "stronger"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The sentence 'My car is faster than his' uses a comparative adjective.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The word 'faster' is indeed a comparative adjective used to compare the speeds of two cars.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Fill in the blank: 'Out of all the students, Maria is the _____.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Smartest' is the superlative form of 'smart,' used to indicate that Maria is the smartest among all students.", "correctAnswer": "smartest"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_11", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["He works more efficiently than before.", "She speaks more slowly than her peers.", "They play better than me.", "I run more quick."], "question": "Which of the following sentences uses a comparative adverb incorrectly?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'I run more quick' is incorrect; it should be 'I run more quickly,' as 'quickly' is the correct adverb form.", "correctAnswer": "I run more quick."}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_12", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the comparative form of 'happy'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Happier' is the comparative form used to compare the happiness of two subjects.", "correctAnswer": "happier"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "The sentence 'She is the best dancer in the class' uses a comparative form.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This sentence uses the superlative form 'best' to indicate she is the top dancer compared to all others in the class.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Fill in the blank: 'John is _____ than his brother at math.'", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Better' is the comparative form of 'good' and is used to compare John's math skills to his brother's.", "correctAnswer": "better"}, {"id": "q_1773574173089_15", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["This is the better option.", "He is the more talented player.", "She is the most creative artist here.", "They are the more reliable team."], "question": "Which of the following sentences correctly compares three items using a superlative?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The sentence correctly uses 'most creative' to compare her creativity against all others in the group.", "correctAnswer": "She is the mo