 all its tenses.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'To go' is an irregular verb, meaning it does not follow a consistent pattern, especially in the past tense ('went').", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "She __________ (to read) a book when I called her.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The past continuous tense 'was reading' indicates that the action was ongoing at the time of the call.", "correctAnswer": "was reading"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the past participle form of the verb 'to drink'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The past participle of 'to drink' is 'drunk', which is used in perfect tenses.", "correctAnswer": "drunk"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["If I was a bird, I would fly.", "If he were taller, he could reach the shelf.", "If she goes, I will follow.", "If it rains, we will stay inside."], "question": "Choose the sentence where the verb is in the correct subjunctive mood.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The subjunctive mood is used for hypothetical situations, and 'were' is the correct form when expressing such a condition.", "correctAnswer": "If he were taller, he could reach the shelf."}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The verb 'to have' can only be used as a main verb.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'To have' can act as both a main verb and an auxiliary verb, as in 'I have finished my homework.'", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "They __________ (to travel) to Europe last summer.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The past tense of 'to travel' is 'traveled', which is used here to indicate that the action occurred in the past.", "correctAnswer": "traveled"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the infinitive form of the verb that means 'to make a sound with a musical instrument'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The infinitive form of the verb is 'to play', which describes the action of making music.", "correctAnswer": "to play"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["She can sings well.", "He should to study more.", "They must finish their project.", "I may goes to the party."], "question": "Identify the sentence that uses a modal verb correctly.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Modal verbs like 'must' are used with the base form of the verb, which is 'finish' in this case.", "correctAnswer": "They must finish their project."}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "The verb 'to teach' is a transitive verb.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A transitive verb requires a direct object to complete its meaning, as in 'She teaches mathematics.'", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "He __________ (to learn) Spanish for two years.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The present perfect continuous tense 'has been learning' emphasizes the duration of the action up to now.", "correctAnswer": "has been learning"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the third-person singular present form of the verb 'to go'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'Goes' is the correct third-person singular present form of 'to go', conforming to the subject-verb agreement.", "correctAnswer": "goes"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["I buy a car last year.", "I have bought a car.", "I am buying a car now.", "I will buy a car."], "question": "Which sentence correctly uses the verb 'to buy' in the present perfect tense?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The present perfect tense is formed with 'have' plus the past participle, which for 'to buy' is 'bought'.", "correctAnswer": "I have bought a car."}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "The verb 'to see' is a regular verb.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'To see' is an irregular verb because its past tense form is 'saw' and its past participle is 'seen', which do not follow the regular pattern.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "She __________ (to finish) her homework before dinner.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The past tense 'finished' is used here to indicate that the action was completed before dinner.", "correctAnswer": "finished"}, {"id": "q_1773671804170_19", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the base form of the verb that means 'to create or produce something'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "'To make' is the base form of the verb that signifies the act of creating or producing.", "correctAnswer": "to make"}]	none	2026-03-16 14:36:44.182403	\N
