ultural transmission in Setswana, allowing for the preservation of heritage and communal values.", "correctAnswer": "Storytelling preserves history, teaches morals, and entertains, playing a crucial role in cultural identity."}, {"id": "q_1773671969673_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Ngwaga", "Ngwedi", "Naga", "Nngwe"], "question": "What is the Setswana term for 'moon'?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "'Ngwedi' refers to the 'moon' in Setswana, which plays a significant role in cultural symbolism and timekeeping.", "correctAnswer": "Ngwedi"}, {"id": "q_1773671969673_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "The Setswana language is a member of the Bantu language family.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Setswana is classified as a Bantu language, sharing linguistic features with other languages in this family.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773671969673_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "To express 'goodbye' in Setswana, one might say __________.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "'Sala sentle' means 'goodbye' in Setswana, emphasizing the importance of farewells in social interactions.", "correctAnswer": "Sala sentle"}]	none	2026-03-16 14:39:29.684946	\N
d74eaca2-e9aa-4bd3-b374-c285cdd8f6f6	694bf5ac-a336-4d3b-9bfb-122692d83f86	special numbers - Easy	special numbers	easy	[{"id": "q_1773679225684_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "question": "What is the smallest prime number?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A prime number is defined as a natural number greater than 1 that cannot be formed by multiplying two smaller natural numbers. The number 2 is the smallest and only even prime number.", "correctAnswer": "2"}, {"id": "q_1773679225684_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "All even numbers are composite numbers.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An even number is any integer that is divisible by 2. While most even numbers are composite (having factors other than 1 and itself), the number 2 is an even number that is also prime.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773679225684_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The number ______ is known as the factorial of 5 (5!).", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The factorial of a number n (n!) is the product of all positive integers up to n. For 5!, it is 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 120.", "correctAnswer": "120"}, {"id": "q_1773679225684_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What do you call a number that is divisible only by 1 and itself?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that cannot be formed by multiplying two smaller natural numbers. They are fundamental in number theory due to their role as the building blocks of integers.", "correctAnswer": "Prime number"}, {"id": "q_1773679225684_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["8", "9", "10", "11"], "question": "Which of the following is a perfect square?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A perfect square is an integer that is the square of an integer. The number 9 is a perfect square because it can be expressed as 3 × 3.", "correctAnswer": "9"}]	none	2026-03-16 16:40:25.779702	\N
