 withdraw from the war on the Eastern Front, which led to a temporary military advantage. However, this shift and the subsequent challenges of a prolonged war exacerbated discontent within Germany, fueling revolutionary movements.", "correctAnswer": "The Treaty of Brest-Litovsk allowed Germany to shift its focus to the Western Front by freeing up troops from the Eastern Front, which contributed to increased unrest and revolutionary sentiments in Germany."}, {"id": "q_1773770584251_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["To establish a democratic government", "To create a socialist state", "To maintain the monarchy", "To negotiate peace with the Allies"], "question": "What was the main goal of the Spartacist League during the German Revolution of 1918?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Spartacist League, led by Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht, aimed to establish a socialist state in Germany, inspired by the Russian Revolution. They believed that a radical restructuring of society was necessary to address the inequalities and injustices prevalent at the time.", "correctAnswer": "To create a socialist state"}]	none	2026-03-17 18:03:04.262389	\N
