on": "The multiplication of 3 and 0.5 equals 1.5.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This statement is true. 3 multiplied by 0.5 equals 1.5 because 0.5 is half of 1.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773842870673_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The product of 5 and __ is 100.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "To find the missing number, divide 100 by 5, which equals 20.", "correctAnswer": "20"}, {"id": "q_1773842870673_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "If a car travels 60 miles per hour, how far will it go in 3 hours?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "To find the distance, multiply speed (60 miles/hour) by time (3 hours): 60 x 3 = 180 miles.", "correctAnswer": "180"}, {"id": "q_1773842870673_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["70", "72", "74", "76"], "question": "What is the result of 14 multiplied by 5?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "14 times 5 equals 70. This can be confirmed by breaking it down: 14 x 5 = 70.", "correctAnswer": "70"}, {"id": "q_1773842870673_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "The product of two prime numbers is always a prime number.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "This statement is false. The product of two prime numbers is a composite number unless one of the primes is 1.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773842870673_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "If 8 times __ equals 64, then __ is equal to __.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "To find the missing number, divide 64 by 8, which equals 8.", "correctAnswer": "8"}, {"id": "q_1773842870673_19", "type": "short_answer", "question": "You buy 4 packs of gum and each pack contains 5 pieces. How many pieces of gum do you have?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "You multiply the number of packs (4) by the number of pieces in each pack (5): 4 x 5 = 20.", "correctAnswer": "20"}]	none	2026-03-18 14:07:50.683965	\N
