 natural numbers. 7 is a prime number.", "correctAnswer": "prime"}, {"id": "q_1773901462746_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is 15 divided by 3?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Division is the process of finding out how many times one number is contained within another. 15 divided by 3 equals 5.", "correctAnswer": "5"}, {"id": "q_1773901462746_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["1", "3", "4", "5"], "question": "Which of the following is an even number?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Even numbers are integers that can be divided by 2 without a remainder. 4 is the only even number in this list.", "correctAnswer": "4"}, {"id": "q_1773901462746_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "The sum of any two odd numbers is an odd number.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The sum of two odd numbers is always even. For example, 3 + 5 = 8, which is even.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-19 06:24:22.832769	\N
