c table have similar chemical properties.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Elements in the same group (or column) of the periodic table often exhibit similar chemical behaviors due to having the same number of valence electrons.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773843747779_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The smallest unit of an element is called an __________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An atom is the basic building block of matter and represents the smallest unit of an element that retains its chemical properties.", "correctAnswer": "atom"}, {"id": "q_1773843747779_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the primary gas found in the Earth's atmosphere?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Nitrogen makes up about 78% of the Earth's atmosphere and is essential for the growth of living organisms, as it is a key component of proteins.", "correctAnswer": "Nitrogen"}, {"id": "q_1773843747779_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Solid", "Liquid", "Gas", "Plasma"], "question": "Which state of matter has a definite shape and volume?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Solids have a definite shape and volume because their particles are closely packed together and vibrate in fixed positions.", "correctAnswer": "Solid"}, {"id": "q_1773843747779_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Chemical reactions involve the breaking and forming of bonds between atoms.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "In chemical reactions, bonds between atoms are broken and new bonds are formed, resulting in the transformation of reactants into products.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-18 14:22:27.791274	\N
3e274ffe-a22f-40ae-b169-7554a96e40e9	dae66086-05af-4c53-9bb0-b68d82239fe1	Biology for Form2 - Medium	Biology for Form2	medium	[{"id": "q_1773844142641_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Energy production", "Protein synthesis", "DNA replication", "Cell division"], "question": "What is the primary function of the ribosome in a cell?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Ribosomes are the cellular structures responsible for synthesizing proteins by translating messenger RNA (mRNA). They read the sequence of mRNA and assemble the corresponding amino acids into polypeptide chains, which then fold into functional proteins.", "correctAnswer": "Protein synthesis"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "Photosynthesis occurs in animal cells.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. This process occurs in chloroplasts, which are not present in animal cells.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The basic unit of life is the _____ .", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Cells are considered the basic unit of life because they are the smallest structures that can perform all life processes, including metabolism, growth, and reproduction.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Explain the role of enzymes in biological reactions.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Enzymes are proteins that facilitate and accelerate chemical reactions in the body without being consumed in the process. They are crucial for various biological functions, including digestion and metabolism.", "correctAnswer": "Enzymes act as catalysts that speed up biochemical reactions by lowering the activation energy required for the reaction to occur."}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Nucleus", "Cell membrane", "Cytoplasm", "Mitochondria"], "question": "Which part of the cell is responsible for controlling the movement of substances in and out?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The cell membrane is a selectively permeable barrier that regulates the entry and exit of substances, thereby maintaining the internal environment of the cell.", "correctAnswer": "Cell membrane"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "All living organisms reproduce sexually.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "While many organisms reproduce sexually, others reproduce asexually, such as bacteria and certain plants, where no sexual reproduction is involved.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In humans, the organ responsible for detoxifying harmful substances is the _____ .", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The liver plays a critical role in detoxifying chemicals and metabolizing drugs. It processes nutrients absorbed from the digestive tract and produces bile to help digest fats.", "correctAnswer": "liver"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the significance of the DNA double helix structure?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The double helix shape ensures that the genetic information is compactly stored and that it can be accurately replicated, which is essential for inheritance and cellular function.", "correctAnswer": "The double helix structure of DNA allows for the stable storage of genetic information and provides a mechanism for replication during cell division."}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Diffusion", "Osmosis", "Active transport", "Endocytosis"], "question": "Which process is responsible for the movement of water across a selectively permeable membrane?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Osmosis is the process by which water molecules move from an area of lower solute concentration to an area of higher solute concentration through a selectively permeable membrane, helping to maintain cellular homeostasis.", "correctAnswer": "Osmosis"}, {"id": "q_1773844142641_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Genetic variation is primarily introduced through asexual reproduction.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Genetic variation is primarily introduced through sexual reproduction, where genetic material from two parents combines. Asexual reproduction typically results in offspring that are genetically identical to the parent.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-18 14:29:02.652024	\N
0f646a98-4343-495b-b939-a1936e4ec126	192d9737-8017-48ec-abf3-ff823bad0d7f	metamorphic rocks - Easy	metamorphic rocks	easy	[{"id": "q_1773844583971_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Melting", "Weathering", "Heat and pressure", "Erosion"], "question": "What is the primary process that forms metamorphic rocks?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Metamorphic rocks are formed through the alteration of existing rocks (igneous, sedimentary, or other metamorphic rocks) due to high heat, pressure, or chemically active fluids, without the rock melting.", "correctAnswer": "Heat and pressure"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "Metamorphic rocks can only form from igneous rocks.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Metamorphic rocks can form from any type of rock, including igneous, sedimentary, and even other metamorphic rocks, under conditions of heat and pressure.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "Metamorphic rocks that are formed from limestone are known as __________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Limestone, when subjected to heat and pressure, transforms into marble, a common type of metamorphic rock prized for its beauty.", "correctAnswer": "marble"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name one common type of metamorphic rock.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Slate is a common metamorphic rock formed from shale under heat and pressure, often used for roofing and flooring.", "correctAnswer": "slate"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Fossils", "Layering", "Banding", "Air bubbles"], "question": "Which of the following is a characteristic feature of metamorphic rocks?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Banding is a characteristic feature of some metamorphic rocks, indicating the alignment of minerals under directional pressure, unlike sedimentary rocks which may show layering.", "correctAnswer": "Banding"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "Metamorphic rocks can be formed from sedimentary rocks.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Sedimentary rocks can undergo metamorphism due to increased temperature and pressure, transforming into metamorphic rocks.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process of changing one type of rock into another due to heat and pressure is called __________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Metamorphism is the process by which existing rocks are transformed into metamorphic rocks under heat and pressure or chemically active fluids.", "correctAnswer": "metamorphism"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What type of metamorphic rock is formed from granite?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Gneiss is a high-grade metamorphic rock formed from granite, characterized by its banded appearance due to the segregation of mineral grains.", "correctAnswer": "gneiss"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["No visible layers", "Visible layers or bands", "Composed of large crystals", "Contains bubbles"], "question": "Which of the following describes a foliated metamorphic rock?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Foliated metamorphic rocks exhibit a layered or banded appearance due to the alignment of minerals under pressure, unlike non-foliated rocks which do not show this characteristic.", "correctAnswer": "Visible layers or bands"}, {"id": "q_1773844583971_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "All metamorphic rocks are formed at depths below the Earth's surface.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "While many metamorphic rocks form at significant depths, they can also form at shallower depths due to tectonic activity, heat from nearby magma, or other geological processes.", "correctAnswer": "False"}]	none	2026-03-18 14:36:23.982964	\N
