me. Here, Distance = 60 km/h × 2.5 h = 150 km. This question helps understand the relationship between speed, distance, and time.", "correctAnswer": "150 km"}]	none	2026-03-18 17:47:57.028696	\N
7ab2c9b0-e695-4b24-b64f-d12e6c8b30a0	977d0a6d-b441-4d36-939a-a6af1ce65c84	biology - Easy	biology	easy	[{"id": "q_1773856210214_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Atom", "Cell", "Molecule", "Organ"], "question": "What is the basic unit of life?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The cell is considered the basic unit of life as it is the smallest structure that can carry out all functions necessary for life.", "correctAnswer": "Cell"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "Photosynthesis occurs in the mitochondria of plant cells.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Photosynthesis occurs in the chloroplasts of plant cells, not in the mitochondria, which are responsible for cellular respiration.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process by which cells divide to produce two identical daughter cells is called ________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Mitosis is the process of cell division that results in two genetically identical daughter cells, essential for growth and repair.", "correctAnswer": "mitosis"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the function of the ribosomes in a cell?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Ribosomes are the cellular structures responsible for synthesizing proteins by translating messenger RNA.", "correctAnswer": "Protein synthesis"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Nucleus", "Ribosome", "Mitochondria", "Endoplasmic Reticulum"], "question": "Which organelle is known as the powerhouse of the cell?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Mitochondria are known as the powerhouse of the cell because they produce adenosine triphosphate (ATP), the energy currency of the cell.", "correctAnswer": "Mitochondria"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "DNA is made up of amino acids.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is made up of nucleotides, not amino acids. Amino acids are the building blocks of proteins, which are synthesized based on the information encoded in DNA.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The green pigment in plants that captures light energy for photosynthesis is called ________.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Chlorophyll is the green pigment found in the chloroplasts of plants, essential for the process of photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy.", "correctAnswer": "chlorophyll"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What are the two main types of cells?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Cells are classified as prokaryotic (without a nucleus, e.g., bacteria) and eukaryotic (with a nucleus, e.g., plant and animal cells).", "correctAnswer": "Prokaryotic and Eukaryotic"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Carbohydrate", "Lipid", "Protein", "Vitamin"], "question": "Which of the following is NOT a macromolecule?", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Vitamins are organic compounds required in small quantities for various biochemical functions but are not classified as macromolecules like carbohydrates, lipids, and proteins.", "correctAnswer": "Vitamin"}, {"id": "q_1773856210214_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "All living organisms are made up of cells.", "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The cell theory states that all living organisms are composed of one or more cells, making it a fundamental principle of biology.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-18 17:50:10.228693	\N
9f61f803-2105-441e-9e58-ee99fd1fa48e	ab81d198-7d0b-40d7-aad9-bf2da113c33f	science - Medium	science	medium	[{"id": "q_1773856245026_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Oxygen", "Carbon Dioxide", "Nitrogen", "Argon"], "question": "What is the primary gas responsible for the greenhouse effect?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Carbon dioxide (CO2) is a major greenhouse gas that traps heat in the atmosphere, contributing to global warming. While other gases also contribute, CO2 is the most significant due to its abundance from human activities.", "correctAnswer": "Carbon Dioxide"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "The human body has four lungs.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Humans have two lungs. They are essential for respiration, allowing oxygen to enter the bloodstream and carbon dioxide to be expelled.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process by which plants convert sunlight into chemical energy is called __________.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Photosynthesis is the process where plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy, usually from the sun, into chemical energy stored in glucose.", "correctAnswer": "photosynthesis"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Name the scientist who proposed the theory of general relativity.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Albert Einstein proposed the theory of general relativity in 1915, which revolutionized our understanding of gravity as the curvature of spacetime.", "correctAnswer": "Albert Einstein"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Solar", "Wind", "Nuclear", "Hydropower"], "question": "Which of the following is NOT a type of renewable energy?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Nuclear energy is not considered renewable as it relies on finite uranium and thorium resources, while solar, wind, and hydropower are continuously replenished.", "correctAnswer": "Nuclear"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "All matter is composed of atoms.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "All matter, regardless of its state or composition, is made up of atoms, which are the basic building blocks of matter.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ is the part of the cell that controls what enters and exits the cell.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The cell membrane, also known as the plasma membrane, is crucial for protecting the cell and regulating the movement of substances in and out.", "correctAnswer": "cell membrane"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the main function of red blood cells in the human body?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Red blood cells (erythrocytes) are primarily responsible for transporting oxygen from the lungs to the body's tissues and returning carbon dioxide to the lungs.", "correctAnswer": "Transport oxygen"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Oxygen", "Nitrogen", "Helium", "Carbon"], "question": "Which of the following elements is a noble gas?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Helium is a noble gas, which means it is chemically inert under standard conditions and does not readily react with other elements.", "correctAnswer": "Helium"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Photosynthesis occurs only during the day.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "While photosynthesis primarily occurs during the day when sunlight is available, some plants can also carry out processes at night using stored energy.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The __________ is the basic unit of life.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The cell is the fundamental unit of life, serving as the smallest structural and functional unit of an organism.", "correctAnswer": "cell"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the boiling point of water at sea level in degrees Celsius?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The boiling point of water at sea level is 100 degrees Celsius (212 degrees Fahrenheit) due to atmospheric pressure.", "correctAnswer": "100"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Earth", "Mars", "Venus", "Jupiter"], "question": "Which planet is known as the Red Planet?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Mars is often referred to as the Red Planet due to its reddish appearance, which is caused by iron oxide (rust) on its surface.", "correctAnswer": "Mars"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "Electricity travels at the speed of light.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "While electromagnetic signals travel at the speed of light, the actual flow of electric current in a conductor is much slower, depending on the medium.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773856245026_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The chemical formula for table salt is __________.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Table salt is composed of sodium (Na) and chloride (Cl) ions, and its chemical formula is NaCl.", "correctAnswer": "NaCl"}]	none	2026-03-18 17:50:45.03914	\N
bf9bccc3-02d4-4678-b038-19a67694f279	ccc51f5c-76c6-40ab-9904-58b03079c40f	ICT - Hard	ICT	hard	[{"id": "q_1773931468214_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["HTTP", "FTP", "SMTP", "HTTPS"], "question": "Which of the following protocols is primarily used for secure data transmission over the internet?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "HTTPS (Hyper Text Transfer Protocol Secure) is an extension of HTTP that uses SSL/TLS to provide a secure connection, ensuring data privacy and integrity during transmission.", "correctAnswer": "HTTPS"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "Cloud computing can be categorized into three main service models: IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Cloud computing indeed has three primary service models: Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), Platform as a Service (PaaS), and Software as a Service (SaaS), each providing different levels of control and management.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The ______ is a framework that governs the management of information security in an organization.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "An Information Security Management System (ISMS) provides a systematic approach to managing sensitive company information, ensuring its confidentiality, integrity, and availability.", "correctAnswer": "Information Security Management System (ISMS)"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Explain the concept of 'network segmentation' and its importance in cybersecurity.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "By segmenting networks, organizations can reduce the attack surface and enhance security policies, ensuring that a breach in one segment does not compromise the entire network.", "correctAnswer": "Network segmentation involves dividing a computer network into smaller, isolated segments to improve performance and security. It helps contain breaches and limits access to sensitive data."}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Bring Your Own Device", "Bring Your Own Data", "Bring Your Own Domain", "Bring Your Own Development"], "question": "What does the acronym 'BYOD' stand for in the context of workplace technology?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "BYOD stands for Bring Your Own Device, a policy allowing employees to use their personal devices for work purposes, which can increase productivity but also poses security challenges.", "correctAnswer": "Bring Your Own Device"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_5", "type": "true_false", "question": "VPNs (Virtual Private Networks) can help enhance privacy by encrypting internet traffic.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "True, VPNs encrypt internet traffic, making it more difficult for unauthorized entities to intercept data, thus enhancing user privacy and security.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The primary purpose of a ______ is to detect and respond to unauthorized access and threats to a network.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "An Intrusion Detection System (IDS) monitors network traffic for suspicious activity and alerts administrators to potential breaches, playing a critical role in network security.", "correctAnswer": "Intrusion Detection System (IDS)"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the role of an API in software development?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "APIs are essential for building modular software, allowing developers to use existing functionalities from other services or applications, thus enhancing development efficiency.", "correctAnswer": "APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) allow different software applications to communicate and interact with each other, enabling integration and functionality sharing."}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Centralized data storage", "Immutability of data", "High latency", "Limited accessibility"], "question": "Which of the following is a key feature of blockchain technology?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "A key feature of blockchain technology is immutability, meaning that once data is recorded, it cannot be altered or deleted, ensuring a permanent and verifiable record.", "correctAnswer": "Immutability of data"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "Phishing attacks are primarily aimed at stealing personal information.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "True, phishing attacks are deceptive attempts to obtain sensitive information such as usernames, passwords, and credit card details by masquerading as a trustworthy entity.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The process of converting plaintext into ciphertext is known as ______.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Encryption is the method used to convert readable data (plaintext) into an unreadable format (ciphertext) to protect the information from unauthorized access.", "correctAnswer": "encryption"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Describe the principle of least privilege and its significance in information security.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Implementing the principle of least privilege is crucial in minimizing security risks and protecting sensitive information from unnecessary access.", "correctAnswer": "The principle of least privilege states that users should only have the minimum level of access necessary to perform their job functions, limiting exposure to sensitive data and reducing the risk of insider threats."}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Extract, Transform, Load", "Evaluate, Test, Launch", "Extract, Test, Load", "Evaluate, Transform, Load"], "question": "In the context of data analytics, what does 'ETL' stand for?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "ETL stands for Extract, Transform, Load, which are the three key processes in data warehousing that involve gathering data from different sources, transforming it into a suitable format, and loading it into a database.", "correctAnswer": "Extract, Transform, Load"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems can learn and improve from experience without being explicitly programmed.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "True, AI systems, particularly those using machine learning, can learn from data and experiences, allowing them to improve their performance over time without direct programming.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The ______ model describes how data is structured and organized in databases.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "The relational model organizes data into tables that can be linked—or related—based on data common to each, making it easier to manage and retrieve data.", "correctAnswer": "relational"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the significance of 'two-factor authentication' in securing online accounts?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "This additional layer helps prevent unauthorized access even if the password is compromised, significantly enhancing account security.", "correctAnswer": "Two-factor authentication provides an additional layer of security by requiring not only a password and username but also something that only the user has on them, such as a physical token or a mobile device verification."}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Contains both letters and numbers", "Is at least 12 characters long", "Uses common words", "Includes special characters"], "question": "Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of a good password?", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Using common words makes passwords easier to guess and thus less secure. Good passwords should be complex and not easily predictable.", "correctAnswer": "Uses common words"}, {"id": "q_1773931468214_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "Data breaches can lead to severe reputational damage for organizations.", "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "True, data breaches often result in significant reputational damage, loss of customer trust, and financial consequences for organizations.", "correctAnswer": "True"}]	none	2026-03-19 14:44:28.226107	\N
