n": "A VPN increases your internet speed.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A VPN can sometimes reduce internet speed due to the encryption process and the distance to the VPN server.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_6", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The primary protocol used for sending emails is _______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "SMTP, or Simple Mail Transfer Protocol, is the standard protocol for sending emails across the Internet.", "correctAnswer": "SMTP"}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_7", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What does the acronym 'URL' stand for?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A URL is the address used to access resources on the Internet, identifying the location of a file or resource.", "correctAnswer": "Uniform Resource Locator"}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_8", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Data backup technique", "Malicious attempt to acquire sensitive information", "Method of data encryption", "A type of computer virus"], "question": "Which of the following best describes 'phishing'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Phishing is a cyber-attack that tricks individuals into providing personal information by posing as a trustworthy source.", "correctAnswer": "Malicious attempt to acquire sensitive information"}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_9", "type": "true_false", "question": "All computer viruses can be detected by antivirus software.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Not all viruses can be detected by antivirus software, especially new or unknown variants that have not yet been identified.", "correctAnswer": "False"}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_10", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In programming, a _______ is a named section of a program that performs a specific task.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A function is a block of code that performs a particular task and can be reused throughout a program.", "correctAnswer": "function"}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_11", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is the purpose of a firewall?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A firewall serves as a barrier between a trusted internal network and untrusted external networks, preventing unauthorized access.", "correctAnswer": "To protect a network by controlling incoming and outgoing traffic."}, {"id": "q_1773931554835_12", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Python", "Java", "JavaScript", "C#"], "question": "Which programming language is primarily used for web development on the client side?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "JavaScript is the primary programming language used for client-side web development, enabling interactive web pages.", "correctAnswer": "JavaScript"}, {"id": "q_1773931554836_13", "type": "true_false", "question": "A data breach is the unauthorized access to confidential data.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A data breach occurs when sensitive information is accessed without authorization, posing a risk to privacy and security.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773931554836_14", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The main purpose of a database management system (DBMS) is to _______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "A DBMS helps users create, retrieve, update, and manage data in databases efficiently.", "correctAnswer": "manage data"}, {"id": "q_1773931554836_15", "type": "short_answer", "question": "What is 'Big Data'?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Big Data refers to datasets that are so large or complex that traditional data processing applications are inadequate to handle them.", "correctAnswer": "Large volumes of data that can be analyzed for insights."}, {"id": "q_1773931554836_16", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Data entry", "Customer service chatbots", "Printing documents", "Manual data analysis"], "question": "Which of the following is a common use of AI in business?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "AI-driven chatbots are commonly used in customer service to provide instant responses and support to customers.", "correctAnswer": "Customer service chatbots"}, {"id": "q_1773931554836_17", "type": "true_false", "question": "Open-source software can be modified and redistributed.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Open-source software allows users to view, modify, and distribute the code, promoting collaboration and innovation.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773931554836_18", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "The term 'IoT' stands for _______.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The Internet of Things (IoT) refers to the interconnection of everyday devices to the Internet, allowing them to send and receive data.", "correctAnswer": "Internet of Things"}]	none	2026-03-19 14:45:54.914432	\N
cab2eb82-8d70-4e93-8487-f96dfd140393	dae66086-05af-4c53-9bb0-b68d82239fe1	Accounting - Medium	Accounting	medium	[{"id": "q_1773932953706_0", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Cash", "Accounts Receivable", "Inventory", "Revenue"], "question": "Which of the following accounts is not a permanent account?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Revenue is a temporary account that gets closed at the end of each accounting period, while cash, accounts receivable, and inventory are permanent accounts that carry their balances into the next period.", "correctAnswer": "Revenue"}, {"id": "q_1773932953706_1", "type": "true_false", "question": "The matching principle states that expenses should be recognized in the same period as the revenues they help to generate.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The matching principle is a fundamental accounting concept that requires that expenses be matched with the revenues they produce, ensuring accurate financial reporting.", "correctAnswer": "True"}, {"id": "q_1773932953706_2", "type": "fill_blank", "question": "In a balance sheet, the accounting equation is ___ = ___ + ___", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The accounting equation is the foundation of the balance sheet, illustrating that a company's assets are financed either by borrowing money or using the owner's funds.", "correctAnswer": "Assets = Liabilities + Equity"}, {"id": "q_1773932953706_3", "type": "short_answer", "question": "Explain the difference between accrual accounting and cash accounting.", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Understanding the difference between accrual and cash accounting is crucial for evaluating a company's financial performance and for compliance with generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP).", "correctAnswer": "Accrual accounting recognizes revenues and expenses when they are incurred, regardless of cash flow, while cash accounting recognizes transactions only when cash is exchanged."}, {"id": "q_1773932953706_4", "type": "multiple_choice", "options": ["Income Statement", "Statement of Cash Flows", "Balance Sheet", "Retained Earnings Statement"], "question": "Which financial statement provides a snapshot of a company's financial position at a specific point in time?", "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The balance sheet presents a company's assets, liabilities, and equity as of a specific date, providing a snapshot of financial health, unlike the income statement which covers a period of time.", "correctAnswer": "Balance Sheet"}]	none	2026-03-19 15:09:13.717413	\N
